    "question": {
        "text": "§\n\nAdverse Effects - Acute therapy (4) : L-DOPA",
        "imageIds": []
    },
    "answer": {
        "text": "§\nAdverse Effects - Acute therapy (4) : L-DOPA\n\nDue to increased PERIPHERAL Dopamine:\n\n(1) GI distress\n(2) Cardiac arrhythmia\n\n(3) Orthostatic hypotension\n\nDue to increased CENTRAL Dopamine:\n\n(4) Neuropsychiatric symptoms\n\n(↑ Dopamine in chemotrigger zone outside BBB ⇒ Nausea. Antipsychotics can be used to treat CNS symptoms)\n\n[Image: 9f652e45a84374b3269736d4ee96a55b8f74125358ac5dcbab68a2659f012f39]\n\n[Image: fbe02242a34f69391049267fc293f10d5cadf6e1eaa63452698cd2c84770e72a]\n\n[Image: 5d7b3c06a150b7d9cdccaef9c5e5f817ff90790bc2b9b7dfa93d788ab6c19760]\n\n[Image: 31df1372c6ac00d35056b94725ed901dd3e303c45895ec04554a823db0efaaad]\n\n5.3 - Levodopa/carbidopa, entacapone, tolcapone, selegiline, ropinirole, pramipexole, amantadine\n[Image: 4c52000b31f9fd212d2c05df63fca40e79e8d7a0cdbe062102b5f34c80adaec2]\n\n[Image: f800f088dc48d94759751b37fecbf710fbe5748729f4fe3267e00c78039d1f39]\n\n[Image: bb7b2fc62457f43096878aa768cc7ee5a9156b0cd10a607ae61eb1e8c87ce013]\n\n[Image: d718d5fe550b992855dd38fc6e58d4669b51d662bd4139833eac03d8d482f703]\n\n[Image: 64fcb46e063f2fe0ea22a5d83f5e357b48a503c46d5b5486580c84f58f7def20]\n\n[Image: 8ec855a71c433ab36ccfa1d63c6b342b86485927e37adacfa5d0bef1074e64ef]",
